* Can you trust it?

    Well? Does a particular class actually work yet? 
    
    *   If you don't see unit tests covering it properly you are looking at brand new code that works 
        only in the sweetest of my delusions. Maybe it does. Maybe it doesn't.

    *   If you see unit tests covering it well, then the basic methods produce about what I expect 
        they should, but that doesn't mean the tests are actually all that good. For example, adding 
        zeroes exercises an add(*) method, but a test of the result can't distinguish success from fail.

    *   If you really care to know, examine the unit tests in the source test folder. Until I get the 
        four-function calculator operating on clados v2.0, that's the best I can offer.

